2
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:38,305
♪♪

3
00:00:49,349 --> 00:00:52,342
♪♪

4
00:01:07,834 --> 00:01:09,826
♪♪

5
00:01:36,229 --> 00:01:38,221
♪♪

6
00:02:10,998 --> 00:02:12,990
♪♪

7
00:02:29,549 --> 00:02:30,827
That's good.

8
00:02:30,851 --> 00:02:33,150
Real nice, huh?

9
00:02:38,125 --> 00:02:39,569
Drop the knife!

10
00:02:39,593 --> 00:02:41,504
Drop the knife!
Drop it! Drop it!

11
00:02:49,703 --> 00:02:51,848
- Get back down.
- Easy!

12
00:02:51,872 --> 00:02:53,416
- Put your hands behind your back!
- Okay, okay.

13
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,951
Hands behind your back,

14
00:02:54,975 --> 00:02:57,053
or the next one's going
to be aimed at your head.

15
00:02:57,077 --> 00:02:59,239
Okay, okay.

16
00:03:01,581 --> 00:03:02,859
- Down, down!
- Everybody on the floor.

17
00:03:02,883 --> 00:03:04,160
- Face down!
- Ladies first. That's it, come on.

18
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:05,628
Come on! What
are you waiting for?

19
00:03:05,652 --> 00:03:07,697
Come on, man! Come
on, fella. Hear me?

20
00:03:07,721 --> 00:03:08,814
Crazy, huh?

21
00:03:13,493 --> 00:03:16,506
Okay, people, Big
Brother's watching.

22
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,692
You move, you bleed.

23
00:03:30,677 --> 00:03:32,288
Ten keys and about
a hundred grand.

24
00:03:32,312 --> 00:03:34,590
We voucher half.

25
00:03:34,614 --> 00:03:35,892
What about Mack
the Knife out there?

26
00:03:35,916 --> 00:03:36,993
He's garbage.

27
00:03:37,017 --> 00:03:38,628
Even if he bothered
to say something,

28
00:03:38,652 --> 00:03:41,030
I'd doubt his own
mother'd listen.

29
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:44,853
Okay... Ed, Harlan...

30
00:03:46,526 --> 00:03:50,540
All right, you voucher
what's in this bag right here.

31
00:03:50,564 --> 00:03:51,674
Here.

32
00:03:51,698 --> 00:03:53,843
Billy, you take
care of this stuff.

33
00:03:53,867 --> 00:03:56,279
I'll divvy up the cash and
give it to you guys at the Cabin.

34
00:03:56,303 --> 00:03:59,068
Come on, let's get moving.
I haven't had lunch yet.

35
00:04:00,107 --> 00:04:02,618
All right, everybody
up! Time to...

36
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,858
When did this happen?

37
00:04:11,384 --> 00:04:12,977
This morning.

38
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:16,799
You mean to tell
me you turned in only

39
00:04:16,823 --> 00:04:19,736
half the drugs and money
confiscated during that bust

40
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:23,606
and kept the rest
for yourselves?

41
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:25,622
Yes, sir.

42
00:04:28,668 --> 00:04:30,660
And this has happened before?

43
00:04:33,006 --> 00:04:34,838
Yeah, it's a common practice.

44
00:04:36,877 --> 00:04:39,856
"Common practice"?

45
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:41,958
And until you felt you
should come forward

46
00:04:41,982 --> 00:04:44,494
because you knew the truth
would come out at these hearings,

47
00:04:44,518 --> 00:04:46,496
you were a willing participant

48
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:49,319
in these illegal
activities, weren't you?

49
00:04:51,858 --> 00:04:53,850
Yes, sir.

50
00:04:55,028 --> 00:04:57,020
Why?

51
00:05:00,033 --> 00:05:01,467
Money.

52
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:07,717
I'm a cop... who
makes less in a year

53
00:05:07,741 --> 00:05:11,234
than most drug
dealers do in one day.

54
00:05:12,279 --> 00:05:14,257
<i>WRTX News at 4:00</i>

55
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:16,259
has just learned that
the Burk Commission,

56
00:05:16,283 --> 00:05:18,461
which was formed
last month to investigate

57
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:20,196
charges of police corruption,

58
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:22,532
today obtained evidence
that it will present

59
00:05:22,556 --> 00:05:25,368
before the grand jury first
thing tomorrow morning.

60
00:05:25,392 --> 00:05:28,137
Evidence that is expected
to result in the indictment

61
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:30,940
of several active-duty
police officers.

62
00:05:30,964 --> 00:05:33,743
Members of the commission
refuse to comment on the rumor

63
00:05:33,767 --> 00:05:37,146
that its star witness is an
undercover narcotics agent

64
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:40,550
who agreed to testify only
after he was promised immunity.

65
00:05:40,574 --> 00:05:43,286
Although... Yeah?

66
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:45,321
It's not me, Charlie.

67
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:47,390
I'm supposed to take your
word for that, candy pants?

68
00:05:47,414 --> 00:05:48,658
I'm not a snitch.

69
00:05:48,682 --> 00:05:50,993
Yeah, he was with
me all afternoon.

70
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:53,830
Besides, the only way to get
hard evidence is with a wire.

71
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:56,380
They put one on him,
they'd have nothing.

72
00:06:04,798 --> 00:06:06,442
Where were you
this afternoon, Ed?

73
00:06:06,466 --> 00:06:08,778
Oh, I was typing up my report.

74
00:06:08,802 --> 00:06:11,347
No, I-I mean right
after the bust?

75
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:13,549
We took the
perpetrators downtown,

76
00:06:13,573 --> 00:06:16,752
and you just sort
of disappeared.

77
00:06:16,776 --> 00:06:18,521
- I went to lunch.
- Well, you know,

78
00:06:18,545 --> 00:06:20,056
Harlan and I, we went to lunch.

79
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,124
How come y... how come
you didn't come with us?

80
00:06:22,148 --> 00:06:24,427
I felt like Mexican.

81
00:06:24,451 --> 00:06:25,817
Where?

82
00:06:27,354 --> 00:06:29,346
Some joint near where we were.

83
00:06:31,825 --> 00:06:34,522
Are you gonna... you gonna
come with us to the Cabin?

84
00:06:36,329 --> 00:06:39,141
Charlie, I just don't
feel like it, okay?

85
00:06:39,165 --> 00:06:41,191
Hey, what's the matter?

86
00:06:42,202 --> 00:06:45,248
Don't you want to hang
around with us anymore?

87
00:06:45,272 --> 00:06:48,451
Charlie, um... these things
always make me a little nervous.

88
00:06:48,475 --> 00:06:51,343
Uh, let me be alone
for a while. I'll be fine.

89
00:06:53,013 --> 00:06:54,190
You go to hell, huh?

90
00:07:09,062 --> 00:07:11,974
Say Ed is the snitch and
he testifies, what then?

91
00:07:11,998 --> 00:07:14,477
We get indicted. We go to trial.

92
00:07:14,501 --> 00:07:16,479
Even if they find us not guilty,

93
00:07:16,503 --> 00:07:18,281
we start looking for work.

94
00:07:18,305 --> 00:07:20,750
He testifies, we're dead.

95
00:07:20,774 --> 00:07:23,319
- My nose is clean, remember?
- No, no, no, no, we're dirty,

96
00:07:23,343 --> 00:07:24,987
- you're dirty.
- Ed'll tell them.

97
00:07:25,011 --> 00:07:28,277
Hey, Ed doesn't care who
goes down, long as it's not him.

98
00:07:30,350 --> 00:07:31,894
- Hey, where you going?
- I'm going to call him.

99
00:07:31,918 --> 00:07:33,396
- Forget it.
- No-no-no. No.

100
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:35,064
Let him go.

101
00:07:35,088 --> 00:07:38,301
Who knows? Maybe lily white
can stop him from testifying.

102
00:07:38,325 --> 00:07:39,969
Commission's still
going to have the tape.

103
00:07:39,993 --> 00:07:43,930
Yeah, it doesn't mean a thing
without collaborative testimony.

104
00:07:49,669 --> 00:07:51,297
Well, boys...

105
00:07:53,273 --> 00:07:54,750
Enjoy.

106
00:07:54,774 --> 00:07:56,470
Money's all there.

107
00:07:57,510 --> 00:07:59,455
Could be it for
a long, long time.

108
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:01,471
Sweet while it lasted.

109
00:08:04,784 --> 00:08:06,195
What? What's the news?

110
00:08:06,219 --> 00:08:07,596
He said he's gonna talk to me.

111
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,098
I'm gonna go over
his house at 9:00.

112
00:08:09,122 --> 00:08:10,900
That's great.

113
00:08:10,924 --> 00:08:12,501
Fi... uh, finish your
beer. What're you...?

114
00:08:12,525 --> 00:08:13,836
Nah, I-I'm gonna go home.

115
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:15,771
You know, I want to be
straight when I talk to him.

116
00:08:15,795 --> 00:08:17,006
I'll see you guys later.

117
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:19,709
Hey, hey-hey... could you
put a good word in for us?

118
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,545
♪♪

119
00:09:58,998 --> 00:10:00,990
Ed?

120
00:10:34,868 --> 00:10:36,512
Hold it right there! Don't move!

121
00:10:36,536 --> 00:10:38,481
It's okay. I'm a police officer.

122
00:10:38,505 --> 00:10:40,098
Well, that makes three of us.

123
00:10:51,784 --> 00:10:54,930
Who had the most shutouts ever?

124
00:10:54,954 --> 00:10:56,532
Walter Johnson, 110.

125
00:10:56,556 --> 00:10:57,867
Give me some hard ones.

126
00:10:57,891 --> 00:11:00,035
All right.

127
00:11:00,059 --> 00:11:02,138
I don't mean throw it hard.

128
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:03,572
Some hard questions.

129
00:11:03,596 --> 00:11:05,774
Who threw the
most strikeouts ever?

130
00:11:05,798 --> 00:11:09,879
Nolan Ryan, 5,297,
September, '90.

131
00:11:09,903 --> 00:11:15,985
All right, who had the most
runs batted in in a World Series?

132
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:19,088
Mickey Mantle, 40.

133
00:11:19,112 --> 00:11:21,047
How do you know
all these statistics?

134
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:24,510
I used to go with a
girl that liked baseball.

135
00:11:25,785 --> 00:11:27,463
Here's a question for you.

136
00:11:27,487 --> 00:11:30,232
Got nothing to
do with statistics.

137
00:11:30,256 --> 00:11:31,934
What was the saddest
day in baseball?

138
00:11:31,958 --> 00:11:35,671
Saddest day in baseball
was the day Babe Ruth died.

139
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:38,174
No, that was sad.

140
00:11:38,198 --> 00:11:41,677
I mean, it's always sad
when a great one goes, but

141
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:45,748
what was the saddest day
in the game of baseball?

142
00:11:45,772 --> 00:11:46,749
What was it?

143
00:11:46,773 --> 00:11:49,585
Black Sox scandal of 1919,

144
00:11:49,609 --> 00:11:52,855
when eight Chicago
White Sox players

145
00:11:52,879 --> 00:11:55,324
accepted bribes to
throw the World Series.

146
00:11:55,348 --> 00:11:56,926
Were you involved in that case?

147
00:11:56,950 --> 00:11:59,862
Trying to make me out
to be a hundred years old?

148
00:11:59,886 --> 00:12:01,197
Well, were you?

149
00:12:09,996 --> 00:12:13,676
You know what a little kid
said to Shoeless Joe Jackson

150
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:15,244
when he came out
of the courthouse?

151
00:12:15,268 --> 00:12:16,745
What'd he say?

152
00:12:16,769 --> 00:12:19,682
He said, "Say it ain't so, Joe."

153
00:12:19,706 --> 00:12:21,584
- Ben.
- Oh, what say, Bob?

154
00:12:21,608 --> 00:12:24,587
- What are you doing out here?
- Hey, Bob.

155
00:12:24,611 --> 00:12:28,357
Well... a cop was
murdered last night.

156
00:12:28,381 --> 00:12:30,593
- Yeah, I...
- Ed Tobias.

157
00:12:30,617 --> 00:12:32,561
Yeah, I read about that.

158
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,496
Another cop was
arrested at the scene.

159
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,298
We got him dead
to rights: motive,

160
00:12:36,322 --> 00:12:38,267
- murder weapon, the works.
- Good.

161
00:12:38,291 --> 00:12:42,589
- Good.
- Yeah, it is, but,
um...

162
00:12:48,468 --> 00:12:51,080
What's it got to do with me?

163
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:52,381
Ben, now, this is
a sensitive case.

164
00:12:52,405 --> 00:12:54,550
We got to make sure
Johnny Bauer gets a fair trial.

165
00:12:54,574 --> 00:12:56,685
Now, wait a minute...

166
00:12:56,709 --> 00:12:58,954
Now, this can't look
like a cover-up, Ben.

167
00:12:58,978 --> 00:13:00,689
- No.
- Johnny Bauer needs representation.

168
00:13:00,713 --> 00:13:02,691
He needs representation strong.

169
00:13:02,715 --> 00:13:04,560
Now, Ben, you've got to
do this for the department.

170
00:13:04,584 --> 00:13:05,984
No!

171
00:13:07,053 --> 00:13:09,365
Well, Captain sent me out here.

172
00:13:09,389 --> 00:13:11,000
He knows we've known
each other for years

173
00:13:11,024 --> 00:13:12,768
and have a close
working relationship.

174
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:14,837
Well, yeah.

175
00:13:14,861 --> 00:13:17,373
Ben, I can't disappoint Captain.

176
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,993
I wish you didn't
know where I live.

177
00:13:25,872 --> 00:13:29,318
Listen, I'll take this, and...
you go change your clothes.

178
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:36,058
- Bob, let's play catch.
- Hmm?

179
00:13:36,082 --> 00:13:38,494
Let me find out what you know.

180
00:13:38,518 --> 00:13:40,578
Who pitched the most shutouts?

181
00:13:41,587 --> 00:13:43,165
Walter Johnson.

182
00:13:43,189 --> 00:13:44,767
110. Ha!

183
00:13:44,791 --> 00:13:46,835
Baseball's not your
game, is it? All right.

184
00:13:46,859 --> 00:13:48,737
Who pitched the most strikeouts?

185
00:13:48,761 --> 00:13:52,163
Nolan Ryan... 5,297. Ha!

186
00:14:02,442 --> 00:14:03,752
<i>It was my gun,</i>

187
00:14:03,776 --> 00:14:07,356
but I have no idea how
it got into Ed's house.

188
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,991
You keep it at your house?

189
00:14:09,015 --> 00:14:10,559
My locker at the station.

190
00:14:10,583 --> 00:14:13,295
According to the
arresting officer,

191
00:14:13,319 --> 00:14:16,765
you were using your handkerchief
to wipe the prints off of it.

192
00:14:16,789 --> 00:14:19,401
He saw me using my handkerchief
to pick it up off the floor.

193
00:14:19,425 --> 00:14:21,203
And he said that
he and his partner

194
00:14:21,227 --> 00:14:26,175
were dispatched to the scene
as the result of a call to 911.

195
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:28,143
I don't suppose
you made that call.

196
00:14:28,167 --> 00:14:30,846
I-I was going to call for help,
but I never got the chance.

197
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:33,115
What were you doing
over there, anyway?

198
00:14:33,139 --> 00:14:34,850
I went over there to talk to Ed.

199
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:37,119
- What about?
- About what he was gonna say to that

200
00:14:37,143 --> 00:14:38,253
grand jury.

201
00:14:38,277 --> 00:14:39,755
I wanted to make
sure he told the truth.

202
00:14:39,779 --> 00:14:40,756
Which was what?

203
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:43,011
That I was clean.

204
00:14:45,184 --> 00:14:48,564
According to what I
hear, your undercover unit

205
00:14:48,588 --> 00:14:51,533
falsified vouchers
and kept confiscated

206
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:53,702
drugs and money
as a matter of course.

207
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:54,937
I was never part of it.

208
00:14:54,961 --> 00:14:56,171
You knew about it.

209
00:14:56,195 --> 00:14:57,840
When I found out, I
said, "No, thank you,"

210
00:14:57,864 --> 00:14:59,475
and I immediately
put in for a transfer.

211
00:14:59,499 --> 00:15:02,044
Transfer, hell. Why
didn't you tell somebody?

212
00:15:02,068 --> 00:15:03,278
Because you don't do that.

213
00:15:03,302 --> 00:15:04,947
Not if you're a cop.

214
00:15:04,971 --> 00:15:06,782
Not when your life could damn
well depend on the willingness

215
00:15:06,806 --> 00:15:08,917
of another guy to
stick his neck out.

216
00:15:08,941 --> 00:15:10,519
You turn your
back, you walk away.

217
00:15:10,543 --> 00:15:12,187
But above all, you don't snitch.

218
00:15:12,211 --> 00:15:13,555
Garbage!

219
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:14,723
You tell the truth.

220
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:17,842
You yell your head
off. You find a way.

221
00:15:25,992 --> 00:15:28,154
I don't want to take this case.

222
00:15:40,039 --> 00:15:41,701
I'll do the best I can.

223
00:15:49,682 --> 00:15:52,428
You may not have killed
Ed Tobias, I hope not,

224
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:54,663
but you've got to
know one thing.

225
00:15:54,687 --> 00:15:57,020
You'll never be a cop again.

226
00:15:59,525 --> 00:16:03,155
Maybe you're not too
old to learn another trade.

227
00:16:08,301 --> 00:16:09,929
Well...

228
00:16:11,471 --> 00:16:14,450
Who knew you were going
over to his house that night?

229
00:16:14,474 --> 00:16:16,218
Charlie Orbach, Billy Pierce

230
00:16:16,242 --> 00:16:19,087
and Harlan Fondy... my partners.

231
00:16:19,111 --> 00:16:21,256
Your partners?

232
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:22,925
Hmm.

233
00:16:25,618 --> 00:16:28,864
Now, the body was found
in the chair over there.

234
00:16:28,888 --> 00:16:32,701
Your client was found right
here with the murder weapon.

235
00:16:32,725 --> 00:16:36,104
Hmm. Did you find the
bullets that were fired?

236
00:16:36,128 --> 00:16:39,308
No, just the one the coroner
dug out of Tobias's left ventricle.

237
00:16:39,332 --> 00:16:42,044
The next-door neighbor
said he heard two shots.

238
00:16:42,068 --> 00:16:43,278
What happened to the other one?

239
00:16:43,302 --> 00:16:45,647
Well, we couldn't
find a trace of it.

240
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:47,182
But the guy had on his TV.

241
00:16:47,206 --> 00:16:48,550
No telling what he really heard.

242
00:16:48,574 --> 00:16:51,353
Was Mrs. Tobias here last night?

243
00:16:51,377 --> 00:16:53,522
Ed sent her and
the kid off to a movie.

244
00:16:53,546 --> 00:16:55,524
Huh.

245
00:16:55,548 --> 00:16:57,759
You know, Bob, this
case isn't nailed down

246
00:16:57,783 --> 00:16:59,995
near as tight as you say.

247
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:01,763
Considering what Ed Tobias

248
00:17:01,787 --> 00:17:03,465
was going to say
to that grand jury,

249
00:17:03,489 --> 00:17:05,234
there are three other men
who had motive to kill him,

250
00:17:05,258 --> 00:17:08,504
and you don't have any
witnesses or fingerprints

251
00:17:08,528 --> 00:17:12,541
or powder burns
or... Oh, almost forgot.

252
00:17:12,565 --> 00:17:16,178
Tobias always kept
a gun... right here.

253
00:17:16,202 --> 00:17:17,913
Loaded.

254
00:17:17,937 --> 00:17:21,683
Clean. Within easy reach of
anybody sitting at this desk.

255
00:17:21,707 --> 00:17:25,020
Now, if somebody unexpected
showed up here last night,

256
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:28,156
what's the first thing Tobias...
A cop... would've done?

257
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:30,259
Go for his gun.

258
00:17:30,283 --> 00:17:32,494
Now, the drawer was unlocked.

259
00:17:32,518 --> 00:17:34,563
He could've got
his gun. He didn't.

260
00:17:34,587 --> 00:17:37,165
Why? Because the
guy that killed him

261
00:17:37,189 --> 00:17:40,369
was the guy he was
expecting: Johnny Bauer.

262
00:17:43,362 --> 00:17:45,340
Well, well...

263
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:54,650
Hey, what's with
you and the door?

264
00:17:54,674 --> 00:17:57,152
- Hmm?
- You're making me nervous.

265
00:17:57,176 --> 00:17:59,509
I'm taking Eileen to lunch.
She's meeting me here.

266
00:18:00,746 --> 00:18:02,758
That's the second
time this week.

267
00:18:02,782 --> 00:18:04,593
Well, nothing wrong
with paying attention

268
00:18:04,617 --> 00:18:05,778
to your wife, is there?

269
00:18:07,386 --> 00:18:09,298
Excuse me,
gentlemen. I-I... I...

270
00:18:09,322 --> 00:18:11,934
I'm Ben Matlock. I
represent Johnny Bauer.

271
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:15,437
The waitress over there
told me you're his... partners.

272
00:18:15,461 --> 00:18:18,040
Yeah, I'm Charlie
Orbach. How're you doing?

273
00:18:18,064 --> 00:18:20,576
This is Billy Pierce over here.

274
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:21,863
Harlan Fondy.

275
00:18:23,169 --> 00:18:25,347
Have a seat. Buy you a drink.

276
00:18:25,371 --> 00:18:26,348
No.

277
00:18:26,372 --> 00:18:27,931
So, how's Johnny boy doing?

278
00:18:29,976 --> 00:18:31,320
How would you think?

279
00:18:31,344 --> 00:18:33,655
Must be tough for him in jail.

280
00:18:33,679 --> 00:18:34,856
How's the case going?

281
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,825
Well, you can look
at it a couple of ways.

282
00:18:36,849 --> 00:18:39,461
Either Johnny
killed Ed Tobias...

283
00:18:39,485 --> 00:18:42,631
Which I doubt, 'cause
he had no motive...

284
00:18:42,655 --> 00:18:47,135
Or someone else did it who
knew he was going over there.

285
00:18:47,159 --> 00:18:49,705
And that would be one of you.

286
00:18:49,729 --> 00:18:52,608
Ed was our partner and friend.

287
00:18:52,632 --> 00:18:54,409
Ed Tobias was about to snitch.

288
00:18:54,433 --> 00:18:57,346
If he had corroborated
what was on that tape

289
00:18:57,370 --> 00:19:02,117
before the grand jury, you'd
all be in the Atlanta Penitentiary.

290
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:03,585
We were all here that night

291
00:19:03,609 --> 00:19:05,854
from the time we got
off duty till around 10:00.

292
00:19:05,878 --> 00:19:07,756
- Just ask the waitress.
- I did.

293
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:10,092
She said you all
came in about 5:30,

294
00:19:10,116 --> 00:19:13,951
but she couldn't say
what time you left.

295
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:16,565
Well, you know,
you're just gonna have

296
00:19:16,589 --> 00:19:18,467
to take our word for it.

297
00:19:18,491 --> 00:19:20,502
You know I won't do that.

298
00:19:20,526 --> 00:19:22,518
Harlan?

299
00:19:24,296 --> 00:19:26,288
Ready to go?

300
00:19:27,466 --> 00:19:29,778
My wife and I have
lunch reservations.

301
00:19:29,802 --> 00:19:32,042
You didn't have any more
questions, did you, Mr. Matlock?

302
00:19:33,372 --> 00:19:36,284
Well, just one more thing.

303
00:19:36,308 --> 00:19:38,800
Hon, meet me by the door.

304
00:19:40,479 --> 00:19:43,725
If Johnny did
this, they'll get him.

305
00:19:43,749 --> 00:19:46,395
Otherwise, they'll
get one of you.

306
00:19:46,419 --> 00:19:48,530
And one thing I'm sure of,

307
00:19:48,554 --> 00:19:51,033
you'll all go to
prison for dealing.

308
00:19:51,057 --> 00:19:54,369
And when you get out...
And I hope it's a long time...

309
00:19:54,393 --> 00:19:57,873
Not only will you
never be cops again,

310
00:19:57,897 --> 00:20:01,777
but other cops will be
looking over your shoulders

311
00:20:01,801 --> 00:20:03,599
the rest of your lives.

312
00:20:15,181 --> 00:20:17,392
May I have your ticket, sir?

313
00:20:17,416 --> 00:20:19,761
Well, my car is
right over there.

314
00:20:19,785 --> 00:20:21,496
Why don't I just go get in it?

315
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:24,332
I have to have your
ticket, sir, and three dollars.

316
00:20:24,356 --> 00:20:25,834
Three dollars?!

317
00:20:25,858 --> 00:20:27,669
I wasn't in there three minutes.

318
00:20:27,693 --> 00:20:29,685
Those are the rules, sir.

319
00:20:35,968 --> 00:20:38,447
Not a penny till
you bring me my car

320
00:20:38,471 --> 00:20:40,463
and there better
not be a mark on it.

321
00:20:49,048 --> 00:20:51,040
Thanks a lot.

322
00:21:16,008 --> 00:21:17,819
How long do you
keep those tickets?

323
00:21:17,843 --> 00:21:22,023
60 days, in case anybody tries
to claim we damaged his car.

324
00:21:22,047 --> 00:21:24,025
Is the license plate
number on there, too?

325
00:21:24,049 --> 00:21:25,026
Oh, yeah.

326
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:26,895
Yeah?

327
00:21:26,919 --> 00:21:27,996
Thanks.

328
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:29,531
Thank you.

329
00:21:37,496 --> 00:21:40,125
The change is, uh, what? $2.50?

330
00:21:42,902 --> 00:21:44,513
Hey, how you guys doing?

331
00:21:55,881 --> 00:21:57,359
Mr. Matlock.

332
00:21:57,383 --> 00:21:58,994
Ah, Detective Pierce, hello.

333
00:21:59,018 --> 00:22:00,162
Is this your car?

334
00:22:00,186 --> 00:22:01,997
As a matter of fact, it is.

335
00:22:02,021 --> 00:22:03,965
Actually, I... I knew that.

336
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:05,967
I checked all the
parking tickets

337
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:08,603
they collected at Captain's
Cabin the night of the murder.

338
00:22:08,627 --> 00:22:12,174
All three of you were
there, but it seems that

339
00:22:12,198 --> 00:22:15,610
one of you left at, uh,
8:30 and never came back.

340
00:22:15,634 --> 00:22:16,611
Is that right?

341
00:22:16,635 --> 00:22:18,046
Where'd you go, Detective?

342
00:22:18,070 --> 00:22:19,548
None of your damn business.

343
00:22:19,572 --> 00:22:21,383
That what you're
going to say in court?

344
00:22:21,407 --> 00:22:24,219
You don't have an
alibi, and I can prove it.

345
00:22:24,243 --> 00:22:26,054
Might as well tell
me the truth now,

346
00:22:26,078 --> 00:22:29,057
'cause sooner or later you're
going to have to face the music.

347
00:22:39,158 --> 00:22:42,504
Just because Pierce left the bar
before the murder was committed,

348
00:22:42,528 --> 00:22:44,506
- doesn't mean he did it.
- That's right.

349
00:22:44,530 --> 00:22:46,675
In fact, the only thing we
know is that his car left the bar.

350
00:22:46,699 --> 00:22:47,776
Anybody could've done it.

351
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:50,212
That's right, too.

352
00:22:50,236 --> 00:22:52,113
Not so hard.

353
00:22:52,137 --> 00:22:53,982
You think you're Nolan Ryan?

354
00:22:54,006 --> 00:22:56,284
Sorry. What's your next move?

355
00:22:56,308 --> 00:22:57,708
Well...

356
00:22:58,711 --> 00:22:59,711
Ow!

357
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:06,294
Since Mr. Pierce thinks I
know something already,

358
00:23:06,318 --> 00:23:08,763
I thought I'd ask you to
go over to the bar and...

359
00:23:08,787 --> 00:23:10,765
Do a little eavesdropping?

360
00:23:10,789 --> 00:23:12,734
- Yeah.
- Right now?

361
00:23:12,758 --> 00:23:14,488
Yeah.

362
00:23:16,195 --> 00:23:17,754
- -All right.
- Wait!

363
00:23:22,668 --> 00:23:24,846
Uh, yeah, Ben Matlock.

364
00:23:27,673 --> 00:23:29,403
Who is this?

365
00:23:30,843 --> 00:23:32,835
Yeah.

366
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:36,658
Yeah, okay. I'll be there.

367
00:23:36,682 --> 00:23:38,493
Who was that?

368
00:23:38,517 --> 00:23:40,562
Sounded like one of our boys.

369
00:23:40,586 --> 00:23:42,163
What'd he want?

370
00:23:42,187 --> 00:23:45,166
Said he had some information
for me on Ed Tobias's murder.

371
00:23:45,190 --> 00:23:47,235
Told me to meet him at the back

372
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:49,237
of the Summit Street
Bakery in 20 minutes.

373
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:51,139
- I'll go with you.
- No, I'll be all right.

374
00:23:51,163 --> 00:23:53,675
- You go on over to the bar.
- After I go with you.

375
00:23:53,699 --> 00:23:55,043
Okay, you drive.

376
00:23:55,067 --> 00:23:56,478
Why do you want me to drive?

377
00:23:56,502 --> 00:23:58,494
'Cause my hand's sore, Nolan.

378
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:36,451
Okay, let's see the cash.

379
00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:38,453
- Excuse me?
- Hey...

380
00:24:38,477 --> 00:24:40,655
you don't get the stuff until
we see the cash, all right?

381
00:24:40,679 --> 00:24:41,856
Now, come on. Let's go.

382
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:45,160
Uh, I-I think you must
have us confused with

383
00:24:45,184 --> 00:24:47,996
somebody else. I...
What is your problem?

384
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:50,512
Huh? Quit jerking us
around and get out the cash.

385
00:24:51,557 --> 00:24:54,669
He's talking to a
gray-haired guy in a gray suit.

386
00:24:54,693 --> 00:24:56,538
Tip they gave us was
right on the money.

387
00:24:56,562 --> 00:24:58,306
Let's take them now.

388
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:00,709
Police! Everybody freeze!

389
00:25:00,733 --> 00:25:02,477
That's Ben Matlock! Hold it!

390
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:03,645
You're surrounded!

391
00:25:03,669 --> 00:25:05,146
Get your hands in the air!

392
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,715
Get down, Mr. Matlock!

393
00:25:26,158 --> 00:25:28,336
All right, don't shoot!
Don't shoot! I give up!

394
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,005
I give up, man!

395
00:25:30,029 --> 00:25:31,806
Get down on the ground!

396
00:25:33,465 --> 00:25:34,709
Get down!

397
00:25:34,733 --> 00:25:36,845
Get down on the ground!

398
00:25:36,869 --> 00:25:38,146
- All right! All right!
- Yeah!

399
00:25:38,170 --> 00:25:40,382
- Down on the ground!
- Take it easy, man!

400
00:25:55,020 --> 00:25:57,499
Damn you, Conrad.

401
00:25:57,523 --> 00:25:59,167
I was safe.

402
00:25:59,191 --> 00:26:02,559
But you weren't satisfied.
I had to be filthy, too.

403
00:26:03,629 --> 00:26:04,756
Damn.

404
00:26:06,298 --> 00:26:08,290
Why aren't you filthy?

405
00:26:09,968 --> 00:26:11,960
I fell in the bread.

406
00:26:28,187 --> 00:26:29,883
It's right across
Peach Tree Street...

407
00:26:37,463 --> 00:26:39,507
Excuse me. Can I just
borrow that for a second?

408
00:26:39,531 --> 00:26:40,531
Thank you.

409
00:26:44,002 --> 00:26:45,146
What happened to you?

410
00:26:45,170 --> 00:26:46,748
I walked into a little shootout

411
00:26:46,772 --> 00:26:48,583
between some drug
dealers and the SWAT team.

412
00:26:48,607 --> 00:26:50,652
Thought you boys might
like to be in on the fun.

413
00:26:52,211 --> 00:26:53,577
Whoa, can't believe that.

414
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:56,639
New look for you, guys!

415
00:27:16,401 --> 00:27:18,713
Chan? Pierce.

416
00:27:18,737 --> 00:27:21,730
I'll meet you at 8:00. Be there.

417
00:27:38,557 --> 00:27:40,549
♪♪

418
00:28:09,955 --> 00:28:11,947
♪♪

419
00:28:58,303 --> 00:28:59,714
Hey, Billy.

420
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:00,949
Morning, Bob.

421
00:29:00,973 --> 00:29:03,251
Hey, I need to talk to
you. You got a second?

422
00:29:03,275 --> 00:29:04,919
Sure.

423
00:29:04,943 --> 00:29:06,154
Uh, not out here, though.

424
00:29:06,178 --> 00:29:08,443
Uh, come on.

425
00:29:23,295 --> 00:29:24,939
Have a seat, Billy.

426
00:29:24,963 --> 00:29:27,609
What's going on?

427
00:29:27,633 --> 00:29:30,111
Well, Mr. Chan here
says you were with him

428
00:29:30,135 --> 00:29:31,879
the night Ed Tobias
was murdered.

429
00:29:31,903 --> 00:29:33,281
Were you?

430
00:29:33,305 --> 00:29:34,649
Yeah.

431
00:29:34,673 --> 00:29:36,818
Why'd you tell me
that you were with your

432
00:29:36,842 --> 00:29:39,334
friends at that bar all night?

433
00:29:40,846 --> 00:29:44,292
Because Bobby here is one
of my informants, all right?

434
00:29:44,316 --> 00:29:46,294
I met with him so he
could give me the name

435
00:29:46,318 --> 00:29:47,629
of a couple new players.

436
00:29:47,653 --> 00:29:48,997
I didn't tell you about it,

437
00:29:49,021 --> 00:29:50,999
because if words gets
out he's on the payroll,

438
00:29:51,023 --> 00:29:53,301
he's dead meat. Okay?

439
00:29:53,325 --> 00:29:55,536
Everybody happy now?

440
00:29:55,560 --> 00:29:57,538
Good.

441
00:29:57,562 --> 00:30:00,842
Mr. Chan's not your
snitch, Billy; he's your buyer.

442
00:30:00,866 --> 00:30:03,878
He buys the stuff you don't
voucher when you make a bust.

443
00:30:03,902 --> 00:30:07,532
Hey, look, I don't know what
the hell you're talking about.

444
00:30:08,540 --> 00:30:10,184
Hey, tell them.

445
00:30:10,208 --> 00:30:12,353
Tell them how
you're my informant.

446
00:30:12,377 --> 00:30:13,988
It's all right.

447
00:30:14,012 --> 00:30:15,990
You shouldn't have
beat on me like that, man.

448
00:30:16,014 --> 00:30:17,992
I don't like that,
you understand?

449
00:30:18,016 --> 00:30:20,110
I told them the truth.

450
00:30:21,153 --> 00:30:22,664
He's lying.

451
00:30:22,688 --> 00:30:24,732
- I don't think so.
- Hey...

452
00:30:24,756 --> 00:30:27,168
Look, believe whatever
you want to believe.

453
00:30:27,192 --> 00:30:28,870
Either way, I got
an airtight alibi

454
00:30:28,894 --> 00:30:30,204
for the time of the murder.

455
00:30:30,228 --> 00:30:33,274
Mr. Chan says you sold
him confiscated drugs, Billy.

456
00:30:33,298 --> 00:30:35,209
He's ready to
testify to that effect.

457
00:30:35,233 --> 00:30:38,362
What you've got is a problem.

458
00:30:39,871 --> 00:30:41,683
Hey, what jury
is going to believe

459
00:30:41,707 --> 00:30:43,351
street trash like that?

460
00:30:43,375 --> 00:30:45,386
He's your alibi.

461
00:30:45,410 --> 00:30:48,189
You better hope some jury
somewhere believes him.

462
00:30:50,215 --> 00:30:52,193
He's my informant.

463
00:30:52,217 --> 00:30:54,762
Matlock's paid him to say all
those other things about me.

464
00:30:54,786 --> 00:30:58,266
He's trying to make Johnny Bauer
look good by making me look bad.

465
00:30:58,290 --> 00:31:00,418
Don't you see that?

466
00:31:01,426 --> 00:31:02,904
You're in trouble, Billy.

467
00:31:02,928 --> 00:31:04,605
You need help.

468
00:31:04,629 --> 00:31:07,442
Coincidentally, so
does Mr. Matlock here.

469
00:31:07,466 --> 00:31:10,211
Who knows? If
everybody's amenable,

470
00:31:10,235 --> 00:31:15,264
uh, maybe we could...
work something out.

471
00:31:17,309 --> 00:31:19,787
What? A deal?

472
00:31:19,811 --> 00:31:22,623
Call it a mutual...

473
00:31:22,647 --> 00:31:24,775
back-scratching arrangement.

474
00:31:35,360 --> 00:31:37,795
Let's hear it.

475
00:31:43,468 --> 00:31:45,513
Uh... H... Hi, Eileen.

476
00:31:45,537 --> 00:31:47,181
Uh, is Harlan here?

477
00:31:47,205 --> 00:31:48,416
Sure, come on in.

478
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:49,684
Thanks.

479
00:31:49,708 --> 00:31:51,185
Hey, Billy, what's up?

480
00:31:51,209 --> 00:31:52,754
Hey, man. How're you doing?

481
00:31:52,778 --> 00:31:54,756
Uh, w-we need to
talk, man, privately.

482
00:31:54,780 --> 00:31:56,257
No problem. I'll go for a walk.

483
00:31:56,281 --> 00:31:58,426
No, no, no, you don't have to.
Uh, just wait in the other room.

484
00:31:58,450 --> 00:31:59,941
No, I'd rather go for a walk.

485
00:32:01,420 --> 00:32:02,730
All right, listen, uh,

486
00:32:02,754 --> 00:32:05,333
go towards the park
and I'll catch up to you.

487
00:32:05,357 --> 00:32:07,019
- See you, Billy.
- See you later.

488
00:32:12,497 --> 00:32:14,489
Hey, couldn't
you've just called?

489
00:32:16,468 --> 00:32:19,480
This lawyer, Matlock,
he keeps hassling me

490
00:32:19,504 --> 00:32:21,482
about where I was
the night of the murder.

491
00:32:21,506 --> 00:32:23,851
He's even got Bob
Brooks in on the act.

492
00:32:23,875 --> 00:32:25,353
Oh, so you're
thinking of confessing?

493
00:32:25,377 --> 00:32:26,354
I didn't do it.

494
00:32:26,378 --> 00:32:27,922
Who did or didn't do it

495
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:29,657
was something we
agreed not to discuss.

496
00:32:29,681 --> 00:32:31,259
- Remember?
- Yeah. Yeah, but I didn't know

497
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:32,460
I was gonna be the only one

498
00:32:32,484 --> 00:32:34,562
to wind up taking
any heat on this thing.

499
00:32:34,586 --> 00:32:36,452
Now, I want to know
what happened that night.

500
00:32:37,489 --> 00:32:39,233
Go ask Orbach.

501
00:32:39,257 --> 00:32:40,535
Come on, Harlan!

502
00:32:40,559 --> 00:32:42,437
Now, I got a right to know
who I'm sticking my neck

503
00:32:42,461 --> 00:32:44,572
- out for, don't I?
- Billy, what I'm saying is

504
00:32:44,596 --> 00:32:46,374
I was at the Captain's
Cabin till 10:00.

505
00:32:46,398 --> 00:32:48,476
If you want to know what
happened, go ask Charlie.

506
00:32:48,500 --> 00:32:50,178
You mean, he
left before you did?

507
00:32:50,202 --> 00:32:51,879
He left right after you,
sometime between

508
00:32:51,903 --> 00:32:53,347
8:30 and quarter to 9:00.

509
00:32:53,371 --> 00:32:54,916
You know where he went?

510
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:57,318
I don't know. He said he
had something about a date.

511
00:32:58,343 --> 00:33:00,087
Look, Billy, I'm sorry, okay?

512
00:33:00,111 --> 00:33:01,923
I have problems
of my own, all right?

513
00:33:01,947 --> 00:33:03,745
Me and Eileen are
not getting along.

514
00:33:10,388 --> 00:33:12,789
You sorry piece of slime.

515
00:33:15,427 --> 00:33:16,871
<i>What was your</i>

516
00:33:16,895 --> 00:33:21,230
relationship to the
deceased, uh, Ed Tobias?

517
00:33:22,267 --> 00:33:24,011
He was my partner.

518
00:33:24,035 --> 00:33:27,381
And your undercover unit would

519
00:33:27,405 --> 00:33:30,284
feign interest in, uh,
buying drugs and then

520
00:33:30,308 --> 00:33:32,854
arrest the traffickers when
they tried to sell them to you.

521
00:33:32,878 --> 00:33:33,955
- Is that right?
- That's right.

522
00:33:33,979 --> 00:33:35,957
And isn't it true
that you routinely

523
00:33:35,981 --> 00:33:37,959
kept part of the drugs

524
00:33:37,983 --> 00:33:40,194
and money you confiscated
during these arrests?

525
00:33:40,218 --> 00:33:41,496
No, it is not.

526
00:33:41,520 --> 00:33:43,264
And isn't it true that Ed Tobias

527
00:33:43,288 --> 00:33:47,001
was about to give testimony to
that effect before a grand jury?

528
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:49,136
Not to my knowledge.

529
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:51,672
Isn't it true that
he was murdered

530
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:54,909
to keep him from exposing
your unit's illegal activities?

531
00:33:54,933 --> 00:33:57,178
If you want to know
why he was murdered,

532
00:33:57,202 --> 00:33:58,412
try asking your client.

533
00:33:58,436 --> 00:33:59,514
Move to strike.

534
00:33:59,538 --> 00:34:00,781
Nonresponsive.

535
00:34:00,805 --> 00:34:03,718
Witness's last
remark will be stricken.

536
00:34:03,742 --> 00:34:05,720
All right, Detective,
where were you

537
00:34:05,744 --> 00:34:08,523
between 8:30 and 9:30...

538
00:34:08,547 --> 00:34:10,758
the night your partner
was murdered?

539
00:34:10,782 --> 00:34:14,095
I was at the Captain's
Cabin bar with Harlan Fondy.

540
00:34:14,119 --> 00:34:17,331
Uh-huh. And how far is
that from Ed Tobias's house,

541
00:34:17,355 --> 00:34:18,666
you know?

542
00:34:19,925 --> 00:34:21,736
I don't know. I have no idea.

543
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:23,170
Four-tenths of a mile.

544
00:34:23,194 --> 00:34:25,506
I clocked it twice...
Walking distance.

545
00:34:25,530 --> 00:34:29,110
Which explains why you
left your car at the bar.

546
00:34:29,134 --> 00:34:32,380
You left shortly
after 8:30 and walked

547
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:34,715
to Ed Tobias's house
and shot him, didn't you?

548
00:34:34,739 --> 00:34:36,317
I repeat...

549
00:34:36,341 --> 00:34:40,221
I was with Harlan Fondy that
night at the Captain's Cabin

550
00:34:40,245 --> 00:34:42,723
from 5:30 until almost 10:00.

551
00:34:42,747 --> 00:34:45,493
If I told you that I
have an eyewitness

552
00:34:45,517 --> 00:34:48,429
who said you left between
8:30 and a quarter to 9:00,

553
00:34:48,453 --> 00:34:50,364
would that refresh
your recollection any?

554
00:34:50,388 --> 00:34:51,866
Who?

555
00:34:51,890 --> 00:34:54,291
Harlan Fondy.

556
00:34:57,896 --> 00:35:01,876
Now, I'm gonna play a
tape-recorded conversation

557
00:35:01,900 --> 00:35:03,144
between two of your partners...

558
00:35:03,168 --> 00:35:05,947
I'm sure you'll
recognize their voices...

559
00:35:05,971 --> 00:35:09,305
And you tell me if it refreshes
your memory suddenly.

560
00:35:10,942 --> 00:35:13,421
Now, I want to know
what happened that night.

561
00:35:13,445 --> 00:35:14,922
Go ask Orbach.

562
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:16,591
Come on, Harlan! I got a right

563
00:35:16,615 --> 00:35:18,759
to know who I'm sticking
my neck out for, don't I?

564
00:35:18,783 --> 00:35:20,761
Look, Billy, what I'm saying is,

565
00:35:20,785 --> 00:35:22,597
I was at the Cabin
till 10:00 that night.

566
00:35:22,621 --> 00:35:24,599
You want to know what
happened, you got to go ask Charlie.

567
00:35:24,623 --> 00:35:26,701
You mean he left before you did?

568
00:35:26,725 --> 00:35:27,768
He left right after you,

569
00:35:27,792 --> 00:35:30,694
between 8:30 and
quarter to 9:00.

570
00:35:32,197 --> 00:35:35,690
You still say you were at
the bar all night, Mr. Orbach?

571
00:35:36,735 --> 00:35:38,646
All right, all right,

572
00:35:38,670 --> 00:35:40,915
I left just like he said
around quarter of 9:00.

573
00:35:40,939 --> 00:35:41,998
I had a date.

574
00:35:43,041 --> 00:35:44,418
You had a date?

575
00:35:44,442 --> 00:35:46,854
Did she mind
walking? I mean, your...

576
00:35:46,878 --> 00:35:49,357
your car was at the bar.

577
00:35:49,381 --> 00:35:50,958
She picked me up.

578
00:35:50,982 --> 00:35:52,493
- She picked <i>you</i> up?
- Yeah.

579
00:35:52,517 --> 00:35:53,995
She picked... me up.

580
00:35:54,019 --> 00:35:55,229
Ah. Oh.

581
00:35:55,253 --> 00:35:57,665
Well, where'd you go?

582
00:35:57,689 --> 00:36:00,334
Oh, about five blocks away.

583
00:36:00,358 --> 00:36:02,003
Empty parking lot.

584
00:36:02,027 --> 00:36:04,639
Stayed there for about
an hour, and, uh...

585
00:36:04,663 --> 00:36:07,074
you know... talked.

586
00:36:07,098 --> 00:36:10,044
Oh, yeah. Does she have a name?

587
00:36:10,068 --> 00:36:13,004
Yeah, she has a name.

588
00:36:14,005 --> 00:36:15,735
It's Eileen Fondy.

589
00:36:22,147 --> 00:36:24,673
You were with
your partner's wife?!

590
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:28,663
I didn't want to
say anything before,

591
00:36:28,687 --> 00:36:31,714
you know, out of
respect for his feelings.

592
00:36:32,957 --> 00:36:36,519
But I... I changed my mind.

593
00:36:46,137 --> 00:36:48,231
No further questions.

594
00:36:50,341 --> 00:36:53,054
Are you going to
subpoena Eileen Fondy?

595
00:36:53,078 --> 00:36:54,455
No.

596
00:36:54,479 --> 00:36:57,858
I think Charlie
Orbach's telling the truth.

597
00:36:57,882 --> 00:37:04,331
Well, if she's Charlie's alibi,
and Bobby Chan is Billy's alibi,

598
00:37:04,355 --> 00:37:06,467
it's got to be
Harlan Fondy, right?

599
00:37:06,491 --> 00:37:07,802
Yeah.

600
00:37:07,826 --> 00:37:09,437
Keep away from her,
Charlie! Hey, Charlie!

601
00:37:09,461 --> 00:37:11,172
- You keep away from...!
- Hey! Hey!

602
00:37:11,196 --> 00:37:13,256
- Knock it off!
- Oh, don't be such an idiot!

603
00:37:14,833 --> 00:37:15,833
Take it easy.

604
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:19,547
D-D-Did you see that?

605
00:37:19,571 --> 00:37:21,449
See what?

606
00:37:21,473 --> 00:37:23,738
His-his arm's bleeding.

607
00:37:39,557 --> 00:37:44,205
Uh, Ms. Tobias, uh, I'm Ben
Matlock, Johnny Bauer's lawyer.

608
00:37:44,229 --> 00:37:47,408
You were at the funeral parlor
the last time I was over here,

609
00:37:47,432 --> 00:37:49,810
and I-I couldn't give sympathy

610
00:37:49,834 --> 00:37:52,235
for myself and for Johnny
for you and your son.

611
00:37:53,571 --> 00:37:54,982
What do you want?

612
00:37:55,006 --> 00:38:00,387
Well, I was hoping I could
come in and I-look around again.

613
00:38:00,411 --> 00:38:02,710
Okay.

614
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:09,530
The police were here for
two whole days, Mr. Matlock.

615
00:38:09,554 --> 00:38:11,599
I really don't know
what you expect to find.

616
00:38:11,623 --> 00:38:16,003
Well, the truth be told,
I don't know myself.

617
00:38:16,027 --> 00:38:19,240
Um, I understand you
went to the movies that night.

618
00:38:19,264 --> 00:38:23,310
Yes. Ed called me in here
right after he talked to Johnny,

619
00:38:23,334 --> 00:38:26,347
and, uh, asked me to take
Randy... that's our son...

620
00:38:26,371 --> 00:38:27,782
And leave the house for a while.

621
00:38:27,806 --> 00:38:31,018
Yeah. Did he do that often?

622
00:38:31,042 --> 00:38:32,753
- Sometimes.
- Hmm.

623
00:38:32,777 --> 00:38:34,155
He worked undercover,

624
00:38:34,179 --> 00:38:36,557
so I just figured that
came with the territory.

625
00:38:36,581 --> 00:38:38,659
Uh-huh, yeah, yeah.

626
00:38:38,683 --> 00:38:41,295
Did he... did he tell
you anything else?

627
00:38:41,319 --> 00:38:43,130
No.

628
00:38:43,154 --> 00:38:45,199
But I should have known
something was going to happen,

629
00:38:45,223 --> 00:38:49,537
because when I came in
here, he was checking his gun.

630
00:38:49,561 --> 00:38:51,906
Uh, I see. He-He...

631
00:38:51,930 --> 00:38:54,875
He-He... kept
his gun, I believe,

632
00:38:54,899 --> 00:38:57,411
in this top drawer, didn't he?

633
00:38:57,435 --> 00:38:58,913
- Yes.
- Yeah.

634
00:38:58,937 --> 00:39:00,347
I remember because

635
00:39:00,371 --> 00:39:03,551
Randy took it to the shooting
range a few days earlier,

636
00:39:03,575 --> 00:39:05,553
and he put it back
without cleaning it.

637
00:39:05,577 --> 00:39:07,021
Ed was furious.

638
00:39:07,045 --> 00:39:10,491
He made him promise to
clean it the very next morning,

639
00:39:10,515 --> 00:39:13,227
or he wouldn't be able
to use the car for a month.

640
00:39:13,251 --> 00:39:16,597
You mean the gun was dirty
when he put it in the drawer?

641
00:39:16,621 --> 00:39:19,967
Yes. Even I was upset
with him about that.

642
00:39:19,991 --> 00:39:21,084
Hmm.

643
00:39:22,594 --> 00:39:24,705
It's clean as a whistle now.

644
00:39:24,729 --> 00:39:26,674
That's not possible.

645
00:39:26,698 --> 00:39:28,876
Maybe your son kept
his promise, after all.

646
00:39:28,900 --> 00:39:33,180
My son hasn't been near this
desk since the night Ed died.

647
00:39:33,204 --> 00:39:34,982
He can hardly go
into the kitchen.

648
00:39:35,006 --> 00:39:36,784
Did you tell the police that?

649
00:39:36,808 --> 00:39:38,786
No.

650
00:39:38,810 --> 00:39:41,746
I... I-I guess I was too upset.

651
00:39:43,781 --> 00:39:46,182
Wonder how this gun got cleaned.

652
00:39:55,326 --> 00:39:57,037
<i>Uh, Detective Fondy,</i>

653
00:39:57,061 --> 00:40:02,643
would you please tell the
court who Red Huntsinger is?

654
00:40:02,667 --> 00:40:05,679
He's an ex-cop who hangs
out at the Captain's Cabin.

655
00:40:05,703 --> 00:40:07,648
Shoots a mean game of pool.

656
00:40:07,672 --> 00:40:09,250
Aha. You ever
play pool with him?

657
00:40:09,274 --> 00:40:10,718
Sure, all the time.

658
00:40:10,742 --> 00:40:13,854
He says you played pool with
him the night of the murder,

659
00:40:13,878 --> 00:40:14,855
- is that right?
- Yep.

660
00:40:14,879 --> 00:40:16,557
- Says he beat you.
- Usually does.

661
00:40:18,016 --> 00:40:21,662
He said you put a dollar
down on the table for a rematch,

662
00:40:21,686 --> 00:40:24,398
but, uh, by the time it came
your turn to play him again,

663
00:40:24,422 --> 00:40:26,448
you were nowhere to
be seen. Where'd you go?

664
00:40:27,558 --> 00:40:29,103
Bathroom, probably.
I don't know.

665
00:40:29,127 --> 00:40:31,405
He said you were gone
a good half hour, and...

666
00:40:31,429 --> 00:40:33,274
and when he finally
did see you again,

667
00:40:33,298 --> 00:40:35,876
you had hurt your
arm or something

668
00:40:35,900 --> 00:40:37,544
and couldn't play anymore.

669
00:40:37,568 --> 00:40:40,147
What happened to
your arm that night?

670
00:40:41,205 --> 00:40:42,650
Bumped my elbow.
I don't remember.

671
00:40:42,674 --> 00:40:45,085
Yeah. Is it better now?

672
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:46,553
Oh, yeah, I heal quickly.

673
00:40:46,577 --> 00:40:49,823
Yeah, I'll bet you do... big,
strong fella like yourself.

674
00:40:49,847 --> 00:40:50,925
I hear you jog.

675
00:40:50,949 --> 00:40:53,627
- Yeah, about four times a week.
- Yeah.

676
00:40:53,651 --> 00:40:56,397
Uh, how long's it
take you to jog a mile?

677
00:40:56,421 --> 00:40:59,366
About eight and a
half minutes or so.

678
00:40:59,390 --> 00:41:02,536
You could easily, then,
jog four-tenths of a mile

679
00:41:02,560 --> 00:41:05,394
in, uh, under five
minutes, couldn't you?

680
00:41:06,397 --> 00:41:07,374
Couldn't you?

681
00:41:07,398 --> 00:41:08,776
Yeah, I guess so.

682
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:12,646
Yeah. Half hour'd be
more than enough time

683
00:41:12,670 --> 00:41:17,284
to jog over to Ed Tobias's
house, shoot him with the gun

684
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:19,520
you'd taken earlier from
Johnny Bauer's locker

685
00:41:19,544 --> 00:41:20,788
and jog back, wouldn't it?

686
00:41:20,812 --> 00:41:22,523
I never left the bar that night.

687
00:41:22,547 --> 00:41:24,658
That's just what
your partner said.

688
00:41:24,682 --> 00:41:26,593
You sure you're not lying, too?

689
00:41:26,617 --> 00:41:29,096
I was at the bar
from 5:30 till 10:00,

690
00:41:29,120 --> 00:41:31,565
and you can't prove otherwise.

691
00:41:31,589 --> 00:41:33,785
I'm afraid I can, Detective.

692
00:41:36,027 --> 00:41:40,207
I'm showing you a revolver.

693
00:41:40,231 --> 00:41:43,610
I ask that it be marked
Defense Exhibit "G."

694
00:41:43,634 --> 00:41:46,780
And the prosecutor here
has already stipulated

695
00:41:46,804 --> 00:41:49,883
that this is the revolver
that was found in Ed Tobias's

696
00:41:49,907 --> 00:41:52,119
desk the night he was killed.

697
00:41:52,143 --> 00:41:54,488
You recognize this
pistol, don't you?

698
00:41:54,512 --> 00:41:56,023
No.

699
00:41:56,047 --> 00:41:59,059
It was in the upper
right-hand drawer, remember?

700
00:41:59,083 --> 00:42:02,563
He took it out when you walked
into the room instead of Johnny.

701
00:42:02,587 --> 00:42:05,599
- I wasn't there that night.
- He knew instantly

702
00:42:05,623 --> 00:42:06,834
his life was in danger.

703
00:42:06,858 --> 00:42:08,569
He took the gun
out in self-defense.

704
00:42:08,593 --> 00:42:11,605
He shot you just a second
before you shot him.

705
00:42:11,629 --> 00:42:14,208
Only his bullet
went into your arm,

706
00:42:14,232 --> 00:42:15,976
and yours went into his heart.

707
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:17,845
- That's not true.
- That explains why

708
00:42:17,869 --> 00:42:20,014
the neighbor heard two shots.

709
00:42:20,038 --> 00:42:23,417
Only one slug was ever found.

710
00:42:23,441 --> 00:42:28,155
The other left with you,
because it was in your arm,

711
00:42:28,179 --> 00:42:29,456
- wasn't it?
- No.

712
00:42:29,480 --> 00:42:31,959
And you stayed and cleaned
this gun and put it back

713
00:42:31,983 --> 00:42:34,395
in the drawer, so that no
one would ever suspect

714
00:42:34,419 --> 00:42:35,796
it had been fired

715
00:42:35,820 --> 00:42:37,564
and start wondering why
Johnny wasn't walking around

716
00:42:37,588 --> 00:42:39,500
with a bullet in
him, didn't you?

717
00:42:39,524 --> 00:42:41,535
- I wasn't there that night.
- You killed

718
00:42:41,559 --> 00:42:44,338
Ed Tobias to keep
him from exposing you

719
00:42:44,362 --> 00:42:46,340
as a crooked cop, didn't you?

720
00:42:46,364 --> 00:42:50,577
No. No, no, no, none
of it's true, none of it.

721
00:42:50,601 --> 00:42:52,546
Then show us.

722
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:54,548
What?

723
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:56,283
Your arm.

724
00:42:56,307 --> 00:42:58,819
Your left arm that
started bleeding

725
00:42:58,843 --> 00:43:01,822
during the scuffle out
in the corridor yesterday.

726
00:43:01,846 --> 00:43:04,024
I tripped while I was
jogging a couple of days ago.

727
00:43:04,048 --> 00:43:05,459
I scraped it up pretty badly.

728
00:43:05,483 --> 00:43:06,994
That's why I was bleeding.

729
00:43:07,018 --> 00:43:08,562
There's a big difference
between a scrape

730
00:43:08,586 --> 00:43:10,397
and an almost-healed
bullet wound.

731
00:43:10,421 --> 00:43:12,633
I'm sure we'll be able
to tell that difference.

732
00:43:12,657 --> 00:43:14,068
- Just show it to us.
- Look, look...

733
00:43:14,092 --> 00:43:15,302
ask my wife.

734
00:43:15,326 --> 00:43:16,837
Wouldn't she know
if I'd gotten shot?

735
00:43:16,861 --> 00:43:18,305
She'd know your
arm was bandaged.

736
00:43:18,329 --> 00:43:21,708
She wouldn't necessarily
know why, unless you told her.

737
00:43:21,732 --> 00:43:23,223
Just show it to us.

738
00:43:24,268 --> 00:43:26,547
Or shall I call...

739
00:43:26,571 --> 00:43:29,837
Dr. Richmond to the stand?

740
00:43:32,510 --> 00:43:34,988
It was fairly simple to
track down the doctor

741
00:43:35,012 --> 00:43:36,790
who dug that bullet
out of your arm.

742
00:43:36,814 --> 00:43:39,726
All your friends
know Dr. Richmond.

743
00:43:39,750 --> 00:43:41,195
I can call him, but...

744
00:43:41,219 --> 00:43:45,418
it'd save us a lot of
time if you'd just show us.

745
00:43:46,724 --> 00:43:50,217
I don't have to show
you a damn thing.

746
00:43:51,963 --> 00:43:54,007
Okay.

747
00:43:54,031 --> 00:43:56,000
No, you don't.

748
00:43:57,335 --> 00:43:59,780
Dr. Richmond will testify,

749
00:43:59,804 --> 00:44:02,082
and the fine police of
Atlanta will investigate,

750
00:44:02,106 --> 00:44:04,284
and that'll be it.

751
00:44:04,308 --> 00:44:07,588
All I really have to do today
is to show reasonable doubt

752
00:44:07,612 --> 00:44:09,790
that my client
committed this crime,

753
00:44:09,814 --> 00:44:11,692
and I believe I've done that.

754
00:44:11,716 --> 00:44:14,695
One-one more... one more thing.

755
00:44:14,719 --> 00:44:16,730
After the Atlanta
Police Department

756
00:44:16,754 --> 00:44:19,500
finishes its investigation,
I'm sure they'll find

757
00:44:19,524 --> 00:44:24,004
what we all suspect... that there
was a great deal of hanky-panky

758
00:44:24,028 --> 00:44:28,976
going on with illegal money
and cocaine by Mr. Orbach,

759
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:30,711
Mr. Tobias, Mr. Pierce

760
00:44:30,735 --> 00:44:33,447
and of course, Mr. Fondy.

761
00:44:33,471 --> 00:44:35,382
And they'll pay
the price for that.

762
